-- title:
--   Descended Gauss ring: uniqueness of supersingular refinement, q=3
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q = 3$ and a nonzero level $M'$ not divisible by $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, and a finite set $W$ of places of the level-$M'$ function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places for $q$ (rational places, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set). Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the base-changed full level-$M'$ field along $A$ with values in that level-$M'$ field (a valuation subring with surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, together with a degree-preserving map on places), subject to the compatibility that the reduction of a Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ lying in the field is the coefficientwise reduction. Further data: an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; an index $\zeta$ of primitive $q$-th roots of unity; families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to hypotheses summarised as follows: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ consists of the quotients $x/y$ of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction, the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ are the pullbacks of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$ attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ matrices moving $\infty$ to $\ell$, the family is injective and permuted by all such automorphisms; each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contracts to $A$ on constants, is fixed by all these automorphisms, contains an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit for every $a \in A$, and is compatible with $R_0$ in the sense that an $R_0$-integral element with nonnegative order wherever $j$ has nonnegative order and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation ring of $s$ maps into $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, its difference from any $a \in A$ whose residue is the value at $s$ of that residue lying in the maximal ideal. Finally, let $K_0$ be a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi \in K_0$, and $A_0$ a henselian discrete valuation domain with an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image is $A \cap K_0$, inducing a surjection on residue fields, with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi_0$ and $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$; let $F_0$ be the subfield of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing the image $\hat\jmath$ of $j$, with the $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ induced by $\iota$. Let $s \in W$ and let $V, V'$ be valuation subrings of $F_0$, both mapping into $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ and both proper in the sense that some element of $F_0$ lying in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ is outside $V$, respectively outside $V'$, and both satisfying: every $g \in F_0$ integral over $A_0[\hat\jmath]$ whose image lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is a non-unit of $V$, respectively of $V'$. Then $V = V'$.
--
--   This is the unibranch statement for the Igusa $\infty$-component over a supersingular place, in the case $q = 3$: the descended Gauss ring $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty) \cap F_0$ admits at most one proper refinement lying over a given supersingular place $s$. It feeds the corresponding uniqueness statement for refinements of the Igusa ring in the semistable-covering construction for $X_H(q^2M')$.
